# The bundle budget is a product requirement

Gate 6 fails the pull request, not a dashboard.

- **Initial JavaScript is ratcheted at 260 KB gzip**, against a 250 KB target. The app currently ships
  around 255 KB in a single chunk, so the ratchet blocks growth; reducing it to 250 KB is tracked
  separately. Adding a dependency to `apps/web` is a budget decision — check
  `node scripts/ci/check-bundle-size.mjs` before assuming there is room.
- **A 500-node canvas must hold 60fps.** Per-node work in a render path is the thing that breaks this.
- `apps/web/vite.config.js` and `vite.config.d.ts` are build artefacts and gitignored. Do not commit
  them; `tsc -b` emits them next to the source config.

## Running a dev server here

`vite.config.ts` hardcodes its proxy target to `http://localhost:3001`, so a web dev server started
from any worktree calls the API on 3001 regardless of which worktree started it. **Run only one web
dev server at a time**, or two agents will silently share one API and one database. See
`docs/ORCHESTRATION.md`.
